=Draft a professional, empathetic, and concise email response to the customer feedback provided below. 

CRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS - YOU MUST STRICTLY FOLLOW THESE RULES:
1. Don't invent anything. Only acknowledge the facts provided in the complaint.
2. Don't promise refunds, discounts, or any form of compensation.
3. Don't invent dates or timeframes (e.g., do not say "we will call you tomorrow" or "within 24 hours").
4. Don't promise specific actions or fixes (e.g., do not say "we will replace the part" or "we will fix the issue").
5. Don't make up names of staff or managers. Sign off simply as "The Management Team".

Your only goal is to acknowledge their frustration, thank them for bringing this to our attention, and state that their feedback is being reviewed.

Here is the customer data:
